    "narrative": "The heart of today\u2019s lineup rests on the elite upside of **James Wood** (71.33) and **Corbin Carroll** (60.42). **James Wood** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable 4.41 xERA matchup against Alcantara and a significant boost from his leadoff spot, which maximizes his opportunities to leverage that 0.408 xwOBA. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher test against Sheehan\u2019s 3.21 xERA, his ability to manufacture runs on the basepaths\u2014our most coveted commodity\u2014keeps his efficiency score comfortably in the \"Strong\" tier. **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor** anchor the middle of the order, and while both face respectable arms, their situational platoon advantages provide enough buffer to maintain their status as essential starts despite the risk of moderate pitching suppression.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Kyle Karros** (38.49). He narrowly missed our \"Strong\" floor of 40.0, largely due to a combination of a low-leverage ninth-spot projection and a suppressed SB outlook against the opposing catcher. While his base projection was competitive, the optimizer prioritized the higher-order stability provided by **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang**. **Brice Turang** in particular remains a staple of our strategy; despite a slight hit for his matchup against Roupp, his capacity for multi-category production keeps him above the benching threshold. We are closely monitoring the weather and lineup reports for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**; should late-breaking news shift their projected batting order downward, we may need to pivot to our bench reserves to protect our limited game caps for the remainder of the week.",
